    "title": "How Does Carnegie Mellon University Rank Among America's Best Colleges?",
    "text": "Carnegie Mellon University is a private institution that was founded in 1900. In the 2026 edition of Best Colleges, Carnegie Mellon University is ranked No. #20 in National Universities. It's also ranked No. #4 in Most Innovative Schools. It has a total undergraduate enrollment of 7,824 (fall 2024), and the campus size is 122 acres. The student-faculty ratio at Carnegie Mellon University is 6:1, and it utilizes a semester-based academic calendar. Carnegie Mellon University accepts the Common Application and has a test-optional admissions policy. The school's tuition and fees are $68,096. Thirty-nine percent of first-year students receive need-based financial aid, and the average net price for federal loan recipients is $34,550. The four-year graduation rate is 81%. Six years after graduation, the median salary for graduates is $105,360.Carnegie Mellon University is a private institution that was founded in 1900. In the 2026 edition of Best Colleges, Carnegie Mellon University is ranked No. #20 in National Universities. It's also ranked No. #4 in Most Innovative Schools. It has a total undergraduate enrollment of 7,824 (fall 2024), and the campus size is 122 acres. The student-faculty ratio at Carnegie Mellon University is 6:1, and it utilizes a semester-based academic calendar. Carnegie Mellon University accepts the Common Application and has a test-optional admissions policy. The school's tuition and fees are $68,096. Thirty-nine percent of first-year students receive need-based financial aid, and the average net price for federal loan recipients is $34,550. The four-year graduation rate is 81%. Six years after graduation, the median salary for graduates is $105,360.",
